                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-35",
                                    "linecount": 43,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 640.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\n07_adaptive_split_sideband — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nOVERVIEW\nImplements Adaptive Split-Sideband Synthesis (ASpSB) from Lazzarini, Timoney, and Lysaght (DAFx-08, Section 3, Eq. 5–20). By passing the carrier tuba, a cosine-mapped modulator cos(I*sin(wm*t)), and a sine-mapped modulator sin(I*sin(wm*t)) through three independent 4-stage quadrature Hilbert networks, the FM sidebands are split into four orthogonal components: Upper-Even (aeu), Upper-Odd (aou), Lower-Even (ael), and Lower-Odd (aol). Allows independent sculptural control over upper vs. lower and odd vs. even sidebands with stereo spatialization across the sideband groups.\n\nINLETS & OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: Stereo Audio Input (Tuba Carrier)\n- in3: Tracked Fundamental Pitch in Hz (from fluid.pitch~; falls back to internal zero-crossing tracker if <= 0)\n- out1 / out2: Stereo Split-Sideband Output\n\nPARAMETERS (4)\n\n1. cm_ratio\n   - Range: 0.10 to 4.00 (Carrier-to-Modulator Ratio c:m, where f_m = f_0 / cm_ratio)\n   - Taper: Linear ratio. Note from DAFx-08 Fig. 14: setting c:m near 10:1 (cm_ratio ~ 4.0, or low modulator frequency) with Upper-Only sidebands adds tight, beating clusters above each brass harmonic for the paper's signature brass \"growl\"; setting c:m = 1.5 with Lower-Only sidebands (Fig. 15) morphs the tuba into deep sub-harmonics.\n   - Function: Controls the spacing of the sidebands relative to the tracked fundamental.\n\n2. mod_index\n   - Range: 0.0 to 6.0 (Modulation Index I)\n   - Taper: Power curve (x^1.25) for responsive harmonic bloom.\n   - Function: Sets the Bessel amplitude scaling J_2n(I) and J_{2n-1}(I) of the even and odd sideband series.\n\n3. low_high_tilt\n   - Range: -1.0 to +1.0 (-1.0 = Lower Sidebands Only, 0.0 = Balanced, +1.0 = Upper Sidebands Only)\n   - Taper: Linear bipolar tilt. Positive settings eliminate sub-fundamental foldover mud while aggressively brightening the upper brass spectrum; negative settings generate sub-harmonic growls.\n   - Function: Crossfades between the lower sideband pair (ael, aol) and upper sideband pair (aeu, aou).\n\n4. odd_even_tilt\n   - Range: -1.0 to +1.0 (-1.0 = Odd Sidebands Only, 0.0 = Balanced, +1.0 = Even Sidebands Only)\n   - Taper: Linear bipolar tilt.\n   - Function: Morphs between hollow, square-like odd sidebands (w_c +/- (2n-1)*w_m) and warm, octave-rich even sidebands (w_c +/- 2n*w_m).\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
