                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-35",
                                    "linecount": 41,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 572.0, 611.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\n10_phasor_synced_comb_flanger — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nOVERVIEW\nA tempo-synced stereo comb/flange sweeper driven by the 1-bar audio-rate phasor (0 to 1) on in3. Multiplies and wraps the 1-bar phasor into integer rhythmic subdivisions (quarter notes, 8ths, triplets, 16ths) and shapes each cycle into an asymmetric fast-rise / curved-decay riddim whip envelope. Sweeps a pair of cubic-interpolated resonant comb filters across up to 3.5 octaves to turn steady tuba notes into syncopated, metallic riddim chop-sweeps.\n\nINLETS & OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: Stereo Audio Input (Left / Right)\n- in3: 1-Bar Audio-Rate Phasor [0..1] (automatically falls back to an internal 0.5 Hz LFO if unpatched)\n- out1 / out2: Stereo Rhythmic Comb-Swept Audio Output\n\nPARAMETERS (4)\n\n1. subdiv_rate\n   - Range: 1 to 16 cycles per bar (Quantized in 16 integer steps)\n   - Taper: Stepped integer multiplier of the 1-bar phasor (1 = 1 bar, 2 = half notes, 3 = half-note triplets, 4 = quarter notes, 6 = quarter triplets, 8 = eighth notes, 12 = eighth triplets, 16 = sixteenth notes).\n   - Function: Sets the rhythmic rate of the comb sweep within the 1-bar phasor window.\n\n2. base_ms\n   - Range: 0.15 to 15.0 ms (equivalent to comb base frequencies from ~66 Hz to 6,666 Hz)\n   - Taper: Direct delay time in milliseconds (exponentially modulated in octaves by the sweep envelope).\n   - Function: Sets the center delay time of the stereo comb filters. Short values (0.3–2.0 ms) create screaming jet-flange vowels; longer values (3.0–12.0 ms) create hollow metallic tube whips.\n\n3. sweep_depth\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (maps to 0.0 to 3.5 octaves of delay modulation)\n   - Taper: Power curve (x^1.3) into exponential octave scaling (2^(env * 3.5)).\n   - Function: Controls how far the rhythmic envelope sweeps the comb delay time on each beat subdivision.\n\n4. resonance\n   - Range: -0.96 to +0.96 (Bipolar Comb Feedback/Feedforward Gain)\n   - Taper: Linear bipolar feedback with internal tanh soft-clipping.\n   - Function: Positive values produce bright harmonic flange peaks; negative values produce hollow, odd-harmonic phase-inverted comb sweeps.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
