                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-35",
                                    "linecount": 49,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 567.0, 726.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\n11_bode_ssb_freq_shifter — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nOVERVIEW\nImplements a stereo Bode / Single-Sideband (SSB) Frequency Shifter using dual 4-stage quadrature IIR Hilbert transforms (Approach 3c from \"Novel Distortion Approaches for Live Tuba\"). Unlike pitch shifting (which scales frequencies by a ratio), frequency shifting offsets every partial by a fixed number of Hz, turning harmonic brass overtones into either lush, swirling \"Reese bass\" barber-pole phasers (at 0.5–8 Hz) or clangorous, through-zero metallic dubstep textures (at 20–500 Hz). Includes pitch-relative scaling so the inharmonic character can stay constant across the tuba's register.\n\nINLETS & OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: Stereo Audio Input (Left / Right)\n- in3: Optional Tracked Pitch in Hz (from fluid.pitch~; scales the frequency shift relative to a 55 Hz A1 reference when f0_track_amt > 0)\n- out1 / out2: Stereo SSB Frequency-Shifted Output\n\nPARAMETERS (4)\n\n1. shift_hz\n   - Range: -500.0 to +500.0 Hz\n   - Taper: Cubic center-weighted taper (500 * (0.25*x + 0.75*x^3)) providing fine sub-Hertz resolution near 0 Hz for slow barber-pole Reese detuning while reaching +/- 500 Hz at the extremes.\n   - Function: Sets the base frequency shift in Hz. Setting shift_hz near -f0 (e.g., -55 Hz) folds the fundamental to DC (removed by the internal 12 Hz highpass) and inverts lower sidebands for \"through-zero\" metallic gnarl.\n\n2. f0_track_amt\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0% Fixed Hz Shift to 100% Pitch-Proportional Shift)\n   - Taper: Linear crossfade between fixed Hz and f0-scaled Hz (normalized to 55 Hz).\n   - Function: When set toward 1.0 with fluid.pitch~ connected to in3, the shift amount becomes a fixed fraction of the played pitch (e.g., -0.5 * f0), keeping the exact type of metallic inharmonicity consistent across all notes.\n\n3. up_down_stereo\n   - Range: -1.0 to +1.0\n   - Taper: Three-state continuous stereo morph:\n     * -1.0: Both Left & Right output the Lower sideband (Down-shift)\n     *  0.0: Stereo Split — Left outputs Upper sideband (+Hz), Right outputs Lower sideband (-Hz) for massive stereo Reese width\n     * +1.0: Both Left & Right output the Upper sideband (Up-shift)\n   - Function: Controls the stereo routing of the upper and lower single-sideband outputs.\n\n4. mix\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0% Dry to 100% Wet)\n   - Taper: Linear crossfade (50% mix with small shift_hz produces endless rising/falling barber-pole phaser sweeps).\n   - Function: Blends dry and frequency-shifted signals.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
