                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-34",
                                    "linecount": 42,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 572.0, 626.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\n12_adaa_chebyshev_wavefolder — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nOVERVIEW\nCombines First-Order Antiderivative Antialiased (ADAA1) Wavefolding (Bilbao, Esqueda, Parker, & Välimäki, IEEE SPL 2017) with Chebyshev Polynomial Harmonic Synthesis (Arfib 1979 / Airwindows Pafnuty2) and low-octave preservation (Focus / UnBox). Evaluating the analytical antiderivative F1(x) = -cos(pi*x)/pi + 0.5*ln(cosh(x)) over each sample interval suppresses foldback aliasing without brute-force oversampling, while the Chebyshev T2–T5 stage injects deterministic 2nd–5th harmonics that never alias on tuba fundamentals.\n\nINLETS & OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: Stereo Audio Input (works great on both raw tuba and 01_harmonic_isolator)\n- out1 / out2: Stereo Antialiased Wavefolded / Chebyshev Output\n\nPARAMETERS (4)\n\n1. drive_db\n   - Range: 0.0 to 30.0 dB\n   - Taper: Logarithmic dB-to-linear amplitude (dbtoa(drive_db), 1.0x to 31.6x gain).\n   - Function: Drives the tuba waveform through multiple sinusoidal wavefolds or saturates the Chebyshev harmonic polynomials.\n\n2. fold_cheby\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0.0 = ADAA1 West-Coast Wavefolder, 1.0 = Chebyshev T2–T5 Harmonic Generator)\n   - Taper: Linear crossfade.\n   - Function: Morphs between metallic, formant-sweeping West-Coast wavefolding (0.0) and controlled, zero-aliasing Chebyshev polynomial overtone synthesis (1.0).\n\n3. asym_bias\n   - Range: -0.60 to +0.60 (DC Offset / Single-Ended Triode Asymmetry)\n   - Taper: Linear bipolar offset (applied in opposite polarity on Left and Right channels for stereo harmonic spread, followed by a 15 Hz DC blocker).\n   - Function: Shifts the operating point of the folder/Chebyshev curve to inject warm even-order harmonics (2nd, 4th) that fatten the tuba's odd-dominant natural spectrum.\n\n4. sub_preserve\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0% to 100% Clean Sub-95 Hz Fundamental Reinjection)\n   - Taper: Power curve (x^1.2).\n   - Function: Splits off the clean sub-95 Hz fundamental via a one-pole lowpass before distortion and sums it back post-clipper so extreme high-drive folding never loses sub-bass weight.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
                        "lines": [
