                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-60",
                                    "linecount": 69,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 569.0, 1014.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\n14_inst_metallic_comb_growler — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nOVERVIEW\nA signature modern riddim / tearout \"metallic talking pipe\" instrument. Combines three core technologies from the papers:\n1. Delay-Based Asymmetric Adaptive FM (Lazzarini et al. DAFx-08) to inject moving upper-sideband formants onto every harmonic of the tuba.\n2. Pitch-tracked cubic-interpolated stereo waveguide comb resonators swept by a kink-warped 1-bar phasor envelope.\n3. A 6-stage Allpass Phase Disperser whose corner frequency tracks 0.75x the comb resonant pitch, turning metallic flange peaks into watery, dispersed dubstep laser vowels.\n\nINLETS & OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: Stereo Tuba Audio Input (Left / Right)\n- in3: Tracked Fundamental Pitch in Hz (from fluid.pitch~; falls back to internal zero-crossing tracker if <= 0)\n- in4: 1-Bar Audio-Rate Phasor [0..1] (syncs the rhythmic comb whip; internal 0.5 Hz fallback if unpatched)\n- out1 / out2: Stereo Metallic Comb Growler Output\n\nPARAMETERS (8)\n\n1. joy_x_comb_morph (Joystick X-Axis)\n   - Range: -1.0 to +1.0 (Center-zero bipolar joystick axis)\n   - Taper: Exponential octave offset (+/- 1.8 octaves around 2 * f0).\n   - Function: Sweeps the pitch-tracked comb delay ratio from deep sub-octave hollow pipes (-1.0) through fundamental-locked metallic throat resonance (0.0) to high-pitched robotic screech pipes (+1.0).\n\n2. joy_y_adfm_growl (Joystick Y-Axis)\n   - Range: -1.0 to +1.0 (Center-zero bipolar joystick axis)\n   - Taper: Power curve (x^1.3) on FM modulation index (0.4 to 4.6) paired with exponential Palamin symmetry factor r = 3.2^y.\n   - Function: Controls the pre-comb Asymmetric AdFM stage. Pulling back (-1.0) shifts FM sidebands below the carrier for dark sub-grit; pushing forward (+1.0) blasts upper-sideband moving formants into the comb resonator.\n\n3. whip_subdiv\n   - Range: 1 to 16 cycles per bar (Quantized in 16 integer steps)\n   - Taper: Stepped integer multiplier of the 1-bar phasor.\n   - Function: Sets the rhythmic subdivision rate of the kink-warped comb pitch-whip envelope.\n\n4. whip_depth\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (maps to 0.0 to 2.4 octaves of rhythmic comb sweep)\n   - Taper: Exponential octave depth.\n   - Function: Determines how far each beat subdivision whips the comb resonator pitch upward and back down.\n\n5. comb_feedback\n   - Range: -0.98 to +0.98 (Bipolar Waveguide Feedback)\n   - Taper: Reverse-power curve (1 - (1 - |x|)^1.4) for high precision near self-oscillation.\n   - Function: Positive values produce bright, open-pipe metallic ring; negative values produce hollow, odd-harmonic stopped-pipe resonance.\n\n6. comb_damping\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (maps to loop lowpass cutoff from 450 Hz to 17,100 Hz)\n   - Taper: Exponential frequency taper (450 * 38^x Hz).\n   - Function: Adjusts high-frequency absorption inside the comb feedback loop from warm brassy wood to razor-sharp steel.\n\n7. disperse_pinch\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (maps to Allpass Q from 0.707 to 7.2 and wet blend 0% to 100%)\n   - Taper: Power curve (x^1.4) on allpass Q.\n   - Function: Simultaneously blends in the 6-stage allpass disperser and pinches its group-delay spike around the comb frequency.\n\n8. stereo_width\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0.0 to +/- 0.35 octaves L/R comb detune)\n   - Taper: Power curve (x^1.5) for fine micro-cent stereo widening in the lower half.\n   - Function: Splits the Left and Right comb waveguide frequencies in opposite directions.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
