                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-60",
                                    "linecount": 70,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 620.0, 1029.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\n18_inst_harmonic_cannon_polybass — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nOVERVIEW\nImplements the Pitch-Tracked Multiband Adaptive Processor (Approach 6 from \"Novel Distortion Approaches for Live Tuba\") combined with Airwindows Focus/BassDrive philosophy. Because the tuba's fundamental f0 is known, the crossover frequencies slide dynamically with the played pitch at 1.5 * f0 and 3.5 * f0 so each band always contains a fixed set of harmonics across the entire compass of the horn:\n- Band 1 (< 1.5 * f0, Fundamental): Kept pristine and reinforced with a zero-crossing-locked sub-octave wave.\n- Band 2 (1.5 * f0 to 3.5 * f0, 2nd & 3rd Harmonics): Processed through ICASSP 2009 Coefficient-Modulated Allpass Phase Distortion and Chebyshev T2/T3/T5 polynomial waveshaping.\n- Band 3 (> 3.5 * f0, Upper Brass Overtones): Routed into a stereo pitch-tracked metallic comb resonator, then sculpted by dual vowel formant filters (F1 & F2).\n\nINLETS & OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: Stereo Tuba Audio Input (Left / Right)\n- in3: Tracked Fundamental Pitch in Hz (from fluid.pitch~; falls back to internal zero-crossing tracker if <= 0)\n- in4: 1-Bar Audio-Rate Phasor [0..1] (syncs multiband comb and vowel formant motion; internal 0.5 Hz fallback if unpatched)\n- out1 / out2: Stereo Multiband Harmonic Cannon Output\n\nPARAMETERS (8)\n\n1. joy_x_vowel_tilt (Joystick X-Axis)\n   - Range: -1.0 to +1.0 (Center-zero bipolar joystick axis)\n   - Taper: Exponential formant frequency mapping (F1 sweeps 240–910 Hz; F2 counter-sweeps 750–2,625 Hz; Band 3 comb shifts +/- 0.8 octaves).\n   - Function: Morphs the mid/high harmonic bands across vocal dubstep formants (\"oo\" -> \"ah\" -> \"ee\"/\"yoink\") while leaving Band 1's sub-fundamental untouched.\n\n2. joy_y_multidrive (Joystick Y-Axis)\n   - Range: -1.0 to +1.0 (Center-zero bipolar joystick axis)\n   - Taper: Linear-to-exponential drive scaling across Band 2 Chebyshev saturation, Allpass PD depth, Band 3 comb excitation, and F2 formant brightness.\n   - Function: Acts as a master \"aggression / bloom\" axis for the upper two harmonic bands while Band 1 maintains rock-solid low-end weight.\n\n3. sub_foundation\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0% to 100% Locked Sub-Octave Injection in Band 1)\n   - Taper: Power curve (x^1.2).\n   - Function: Controls the level of the f0-locked sub-octave generator summed with the isolated fundamental in Band 1.\n\n4. mid_allpass_pd\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0% to 100% Coefficient-Modulated Allpass Phase Distortion on Band 2)\n   - Taper: Linear modulation of the ICASSP 2009 tanh-smoothed sawtooth allpass coefficient m(t) in [0.15, 0.93].\n   - Function: Imparts sawtooth phase distortion specifically to the 2nd and 3rd harmonics of the tuba.\n\n5. high_comb_metal\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (maps to Band 3 comb feedback from 0.0 to 0.88)\n   - Taper: Linear feedback scaling with internal tanh loop saturation.\n   - Function: Controls the metallic pipe resonance applied exclusively to harmonics above 3.5 * f0.\n\n6. motion_subdiv\n   - Range: 1 to 16 cycles per bar (Quantized in 16 integer steps)\n   - Taper: Stepped integer multiplier of the 1-bar phasor.\n   - Function: Sets the rhythmic subdivision rate of the synced formant and comb modulation LFO.\n\n7. motion_depth\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0\n   - Taper: Asymmetric triangle LFO (duty = 0.30) modulating both the Band 3 comb pitch (up to +1 octave) and the F1/F2 vowel formant cutoffs.\n   - Function: Controls the depth of the 1-bar synced rhythmic animation.\n\n8. stereo_spread\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (maps to +/- 25% L/R comb delay offset and +/- 10% vowel formant offset)\n   - Taper: Linear stereo divergence (Band 1 fundamental and sub-octave remain 100% mono-centered for club/PA sub compatibility).\n   - Function: Widens the stereo image of the upper two harmonic bands while keeping the sub-bass mono.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
                        "lines": [
